---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import DocsSearch from "../components/DocsSearch.astro";
---
<Base
  title="CertMate Agent — plain answers about TLS certificates, DNS-01 and ACME"
  description="Explainers on DNS-01 validation, wildcard certificates, CNAME delegation, deploy hooks and automated renewal, plus a documentation assistant that runs a local LLM over CertMate's docs. No credentials, no telemetry."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Local LLM · Retrieval over the docs · No credentials</p>
    <h1>Plain answers about<br />TLS certificates.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      How DNS-01 validation actually works, when a wildcard is worth it, what
      CNAME delegation buys you, and why a renewal that "succeeded" can still
      leave the old certificate being served. Written for operators, grounded in
      <a href="https://github.com/fabriziosalmi/certmate" rel="noopener">CertMate</a>'s
      documentation.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/topics/">
        Read the explainers
      </a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://www.certmate.org" rel="noopener">
        CertMate ↗
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="hero-foot subtle">
      <strong>CertMate Agent</strong> also runs as a local documentation
      assistant: an embedded LLM with retrieval over those docs, answering in
      your terminal and citing the file it drew from. It holds no credentials
      and never connects to a running instance — to drive a live CertMate from
      an assistant, use the
      <a href="https://github.com/fabriziosalmi/certmate/blob/main/docs/mcp.md" rel="noopener">MCP server</a>
      that ships with CertMate itself, maintained where the API is maintained.
    </p>
  </section>

  <DocsSearch />

  <section class="features">
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Deterministic lookups</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        <code>/docs</code> bypasses the LLM entirely and returns ranked excerpts straight from the index, each labelled with the file it came from. <code>/help</code> lists the commands, <code>/reindex</code> rebuilds the index. That is the whole surface.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Local LLM via LM Studio</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Zero data leaves your machine. Point it at any OpenAI-compatible local model to ask questions about CertMate's documentation in your own terminal.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Nothing to compromise</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        It reads documentation. It holds no CertMate credential, opens no connection to a running instance, and has no write path to anything. The API mapping it once had was removed in 0.2.0 — a second mapping of an API maintained elsewhere could only drift, and had.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Local RAG Engine</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        A built-in indexer chunks and embeds CertMate's documentation on your machine. Ask <code>/docs DNS-01 validation</code> and get ranked excerpts with their source file, without an external API call.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="terminal-preview prose">
    <h2>What it actually looks like.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Three commands, no credentials, no connection to anything but the local
      model and the index on disk. Answers name the file they came from, so you
      can go and read it.
    </p>

    <div class="terminal-mockup">
      <div class="mockup-header">
        <span class="dot red"></span>
        <span class="dot yellow"></span>
        <span class="dot green"></span>
        <span class="mockup-title">certmate-agent</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mockup-body">
        <p class="user-line"><span>&#8250;</span> /docs DNS-01 validation</p>
        <p class="agent-line">Top 3 excerpt(s) for <code>DNS-01 validation</code>:</p>
        <p class="agent-line"><code>docs/dns-providers.md</code> <em>(DNS-01 challenge)</em> — score 0.82</p>
        <p class="agent-line"><code>docs/guide.md</code> <em>(Creating a certificate)</em> — score 0.71</p>
        <p class="agent-line"><code>docs/ca-providers.md</code> <em>(Wildcards)</em> — score 0.64</p>
        <p class="user-line"><span>&#8250;</span> why does a wildcard need DNS-01?</p>
        <p class="agent-line">Because HTTP-01 proves control of a single hostname by serving a file on it, and there is no host to serve from for <code>*.example.com</code>. DNS-01 proves control of the zone instead, which is what a wildcard actually asserts. <em>(docs/dns-providers.md)</em></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-bottom">
    <div class="cta-box">
      <h2>Manage the certificates themselves with CertMate.</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Open source, self-hosted: issues and renews TLS certificates across 29 DNS providers, discovers the ones you did not issue, and deploys renewed certificates where they are needed. These pages explain the concepts; CertMate does the work.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row centered">
        <a class="btn primary" href="https://www.certmate.org" rel="noopener">
          CertMate ↗
        </a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/fabriziosalmi/certmate-agent" rel="noopener">
          This assistant, on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .hero {
    padding: 32px 0 48px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 64px;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw + 1rem, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .hero h1 br {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .hero h1 br { display: inline; }
  }
  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .hero-foot {
    margin-top: 40px;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .btn.primary {
    background: var(--fg);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--fg);
  }
  .btn.primary:hover {
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .features {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 0 0 80px;
  }
  .feature {
    padding: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  .feature h3 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .feature p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }

  .terminal-preview {
    margin-top: 64px;
  }
  
  .terminal-mockup {
    margin-top: 32px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #000000;
    color: #f4f4f5;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px -12px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
  }
  .mockup-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    background: #18181b;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #27272a;
  }
  .mockup-header .dot {
    width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .dot.red { background: #ef4444; }
  .dot.yellow { background: #f59e0b; }
  .dot.green { background: #10b981; }
  .mockup-title {
    margin-left: 12px;
    color: #a1a1aa;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .mockup-body {
    padding: 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .user-line { color: #f4f4f5; margin: 0; }
  .user-line span { color: #52525b; margin-right: 8px; }
  .agent-line { color: #a1a1aa; margin: 0; }
  
  .mockup-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 8px 0;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .mockup-table th { color: #71717a; text-align: left; padding: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #27272a; }
  .mockup-table td { padding: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #27272a; }
  .mockup-table .warn { color: #f59e0b; }
  
  .mockup-confirm {
    border: 1px solid #d97706;
    background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.05);
    padding: 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-left: 3px solid #f59e0b;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .mockup-actions { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-top: 16px; }
  .mockup-btn {
    appearance: none; background: #18181b; border: 1px solid #3f3f46; color: #f4f4f5;
    padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500;
  }
  .mockup-btn.primary { background: #fafafa; color: #0a0a0a; border-color: #fafafa; }

  .cta-bottom {
    margin: 100px 0 0;
  }
  .cta-box {
    padding: 48px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--panel);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cta-box h2 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .cta-box p { margin: 0 0 32px; }
  .cta-row.centered { justify-content: center; }
</style>
